**Neros Archer FPV Drone – All Technical Specifications (MVP Terms)**  
*(Compiled from official Neros.tech sources, U.S. military announcements, and consistent public reporting. Note: Unlike the Skydio X10D, Neros does not publish a full public datasheet with dimensions, exact weights, battery details, hover/flight time, or precise wind/altitude limits — typical for attritable military FPV systems. Only verified/high-confidence specs are listed below.)*

### Platform / Aircraft
- **Type**: High-performance long-range First-Person View (FPV) tactical UAV / quadcopter
- **Variants**:
  - 5-inch frame
  - 8-inch (original battlefield-tested version)
  - 10-inch frame
  - Archer Strike (kinetic-enabled with integrated strike payloads)
  - Archer Fiber (fiber-optic variant for maximum EW resilience)
- **BlueUAS Status**: Approved / listed (first FPV platform on the BlueUAS list)
- **Manufacturing**: Fully U.S.-made, NDAA-compliant options, secure supply chain, no Chinese components
- **Primary Role**: Tactical strike, modular payload delivery, attritable one-way attack drone
- **Comms / EW Resilience**: Custom-built radios with industry-leading jamming resistance; pairs with Crossbow Tactical Ground Station (or Flatbow soldier-borne variant)
- **Modularity**: Fully customizable payload bay; expandable architecture with custom flight computer and integrated sensors

### Performance
- **Operational Range** (no interference, line-of-sight): 20+ km / >12.4 miles (with ~2 kg payload)
- **Payload Capacity**: Up to 2 kg (4.5 lb) — supports modular payloads or Kraken Kinetics Terminus anti-armor/anti-personnel strike modules (Archer Strike)
- **Max Speed**: Up to 160 km/h (≈ 99 mph / 44 m/s); operational demonstrations >90 mph
- **Flight Characteristics**: Optimized for long-range missions in contested environments; high-performance propulsion (in-house motors and drivers)

### Additional Features
- **Ground Control Station**: Crossbow Tactical GCS (rugged, mobile, enhanced standoff and jamming mitigation)
- **Camera / Video**: High-performance FPV camera with low-light / night operation capabilities (exact sensor details not publicly disclosed)
- **Cost Positioning**: ~$2,000 – under $5,000 per unit (order-of-magnitude cheaper than comparable BlueUAS small UAS)
- **Autonomy / Software**: Smart software-defined hardware; rapid iteration capability; battlefield-proven components
- **Certification / Compliance**: BlueUAS cleared; selected for U.S. Army Purpose-Built Attritable Systems (PBAS) program

**Notes on Fiber-Optic Variant (Archer Fiber)**:  
Current configuration uses a 5 km fiber spool (10 km and 15 km variants in development for early 2026). Trades range for complete immunity to RF jamming/EW.

All data pulled directly from Neros official site, PBAS program announcements, and verified defense reporting. Detailed engineering specs (dimensions, dry weight, max takeoff weight, exact endurance, service ceiling, ingress protection, etc.) remain undisclosed publicly.  

